      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "[{(Ph2SiO)2O}2{Li(THF)2}2]EuCl (5) (0.66 g, 0.50 mmol) was added to a stirred solution of (DADDipp)Ba(DME) (0.24 g, 0.25 mmol) in 40 mL of toluene. After stirring overnight, an off-white precipitate (analyzed as nearly quantitative BaCl2) was filtered off and the orange solution reduced stepwise to <5 mL. Small orange crystals of 7 formed during one week at room temperature (isolated yield 61% after structure determination). Neutral DADDipp was detected in the mother liquor by NMR. Formation is attributed to the strongly reducing diazadiene radical-anion barium reagent.",
